<SiteLayout
  title="History"
  description="The history of the National Points Race and its independent automated revival."
>
  <article class="shell hero prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">History and stewardship</p>
    <h1>A national race, preserved and restarted.</h1>
    <p class="dek">
      Extemp Central created a season-long way to recognize sustained excellence in
      high school extemporaneous speaking. This independent project preserves that
      record and gives the race a new, autonomous life.
    </p>

    <h2>The original NPR</h2>
    <p>
      Writer and editor Logan Scisco developed the National Points Race at Extemp
      Central. It grouped selected national-circuit tournaments into five tiers and
      awarded competitors points based on placement and elimination-round progress.
      Extemp Central published ten completed seasons. The record begins in 2008-09
      and ends with Robert Zhang winning the 2024-25 race.
    </p>
    <p class="source-note">
      Source: <a href="https://extemp.com/natl-points-race/">Extemp Central's National Points Race archive</a>
      and its linked annual standings.
    </p>

    <h2>The pause</h2>
    <p>
      Extemp Central stopped publishing the NPR after the 2024-25 season. No official
      contemporaneous NPR was published for 2025-26. The archive remains valuable,
      but the season-long national comparison disappeared.
    </p>

    <h2>Saras Totey's independent revival</h2>
    <p>
      Saras Totey independently rebuilt the idea as an autonomous, open, and auditable
      system. The 2025-26 season is reconstructed after the fact to prove the pipeline.
      The 2026-27 season is the current live race. The successor keeps the last published
      scoring policy, preserves source evidence, reports ambiguity instead of guessing,
      and exposes how every calculation was made.
    </p>
    <div class="notice">
      <h3>Independent, not acquired</h3>
      <p>
        Saras did not acquire Extemp Central. This project is not endorsed by Extemp
        Central or any results provider. It is an independently operated successor
        that credits the original work and links back to it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
